From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 20:52:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports/arkweb: wire HTTP-auth and permission request delegates

request_authentication -> OnHttpAuthRequestByJS and request_permission ->
onGeolocationShow/onPermissionRequest, via parked requests resolved through
new resolve_http_auth/resolve_permission bridge fns. Enable dom_geolocation.

HTTP auth works end-to-end; the permission path is wired but not yet reachable
from web content (Servo geolocation/getUserMedia don't send PromptPermission).

Add ControllerPage handlers, an http_server conftest fixture (loopback = secure
context, + Basic-auth endpoint) and test_permissions.py. The HTTP-auth
round-trip is verified; the geolocation prompt is tracked as xfail pending
Servo-side plumbing.

Validation: Test by running uv run ports/arkweb/tools/test_permissions.py on a device.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implementation and on-device testing)

Require an explicit target when several devices are attached.

The pytest fixtures took `Hdc().list_targets()[0]`, so on a bench with more than
one device connected the suite silently drove whichever one hdc happened to
enumerate first. `http_server` made it worse by resolving the target a second
time, independently of the `device` fixture, so its `hdc rport` could land on a
different device than the tests were driving.

Resolve the serial once, in a session-scoped `hdc_target` fixture, with the
semantics deploy.py already uses for `--target`: a lone attached device is used
implicitly, an ambiguous fleet is an error naming the attached serials, and an
explicitly requested serial that is not attached is an error rather than a
silent fallback. The choice comes from `--target` or `HDC_TARGET`; the env var
is what makes the single-file `uv run ports/arkweb/tools/test_x.py` form
selectable, since its `__main__` does not forward arguments to pytest.

Validation: Test with two devices attached: the suite must fail naming both serials, `--target=<serial>` and `HDC_TARGET=<serial>` must each run against the named device, and an unattached serial must be rejected. `uv run ports/arkweb/tools/test_render.py` covers the single-file path and test_permissions.py the `hdc rport` path.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implementation and on-device testing)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <jschwender@posteo.net>
